1118920

# esbuild 0.27.7 (GHSA-g7r4-m6w7-qqqr low), fixed in 0.28.1. A sibling high
# advisory (1120679) no longer appears in npm audit output and was pruned.
# Pulled transitively by astro@5.18.1 (esbuild ^0.27.3) and vite@7.3.3 (esbuild ^0.27.0);
# 0.28.1 is outside both ^0.27.x carets, so reaching the fix needs a forced override that
# overrides astro's pinned peer range and risks an esbuild 0.28 www-build regression.
# BLOCKER: neither advisory is reachable in our build — the high one is the esbuild Deno module (lib/deno/mod.ts), which we never import (Node-only toolchain), and the low one is the esbuild dev server's Windows path traversal; the dev server is never shipped to prod and CI/prod builds do not run on Windows. Drop once astro/vite widen the esbuild range to admit 0.28.1.
1120680

# astro 5.18.1 reflected-XSS / unescaped-attribute / host-header SSRF advisories.
# UPSTREAM RENUMBERED THIS FAMILY on 2026-08-15: 1120912 and 1120917 stopped firing
# and 1123700 / 1139373 / 1139375 / 1139376 / 1139377 / 1139378 took their place,
# several of them explicitly "incomplete fix for CVE-2026-54298" re-issues of the
# same defects. The dead pair was deleted (the liveness half of the convention) and
# the live ids added; the reasoning below is unchanged because the vulnerabilities
# are. The patched versions are astro 7.0.2+, a major upgrade that removes legacy
# content collections and requires migrating src/content/config.ts to
# src/content.config.ts with collection loaders — tracked separately.
# BLOCKER: @rediacc/www builds with astro output: 'static' (astro.config.mjs:144).
# Two distinct arguments, and they are not the same one twice: the host-header SSRF
# in the prerendered error-page fetch (1139377) needs a SERVER to receive a Host
# header, and a static export has none. The XSS advisories (1123700, 1139373,
# 1139375, 1139376, 1139378 — spread attribute names, transition:* directive values,
# View Transition animation properties, slot names) are render-time escaping bugs,
# and in a static export rendering happens at BUILD time over our own committed
# content, so there is no request-time attacker-controlled value to inject. Note
# 1139375 names hydrated islands, which a static build does ship — it is covered by
# the second argument, not the first, because the directive values still come from
# our source. Drop the whole group once the site migrates to astro v7.
1123700
1139373
1139375
1139376
1139377
1139378

# js-yaml 3.x quadratic CPU in !!omap resolution (GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj,
# CVE-2026-59870). The 4.x half of this advisory was FIXED, not allowlisted:
# the root override moved >=4.2.0 <5.0.0 -> >=4.3.1 <5.0.0, which cleared
# sibling id 1138115 and every 4.x consumer (astro, @astrojs/markdown-remark,
# @marp-team/marpit all resolve 4.3.1 now). Only the 3.x instance is left.
# BLOCKER: no patched 3.x exists — the advisory states the fix was NOT
# backported — and the single consumer cannot move to 4.x: gray-matter@4.0.3
# binds yaml.safeLoad/safeDump (lib/engines.js:16-17), both REMOVED in js-yaml
# 4, which is why the nested "gray-matter": {"js-yaml": "^3.15.0"} override
# already exists. Not reachable as a DoS either: gray-matter is a build-time
# dependency of packages/www only (npm ls shows @rediacc/www as its sole
# parent), it parses frontmatter of our own committed content, and www is
# output: 'static' (astro.config.mjs:144) so no server evaluates YAML at
# request time. Re-check when gray-matter ships a js-yaml 4 engine.
1138114

